# AUDIT SM14 F15 — READ BEFORE RELYING ON THIS FILE.
#
# REQUIRED-REVIEW DEPENDENCY (not verifiable from this repository): a
# CODEOWNERS file only BITES when branch protection on main requires review
# from a code owner before merging. If that setting is off, everything below
# is documentation, not enforcement. OPERATOR CHECKLIST (GitHub → Settings →
# Branches → main → Protect):
#   1. "Require a pull request before merging" = ON.
#   2. "Require review from Code Owners" = ON.
#   3. (recommended) "Require approval of the most recent reviewable push".
# The CI system also posts the required "woodpecker" commit status — keep
# that context required too (ci/README.md §12).
#
# SINGLE-POINT-OF-OWNERSHIP RISK: every path below — including /ci/,
# /deploy/ and .woodpecker.yml, the exact files that gate everything else —
# is owned by the SAME single account. One owner means NO review separation
# for CI/release changes: the person (or a compromised token of the person)
# who changes a gate can approve their own change. RECOMMENDATION: add a
# second owner or a team to the release-critical paths, e.g.
#     /ci/              @sbelakho2 @apexmail-release-engineering
#     /deploy/          @sbelakho2 @apexmail-release-engineering
#     /.woodpecker.yml  @sbelakho2 @apexmail-release-engineering
# (create the team with at least one human who is not the sole deploy
# admin). Until then, treat CI/release changes as self-reviewed and rely on
# the mechanical gates: the validate stage's pipeline-config sanity checks,
# the digest-pinned executor image (audit SM14 F9) and the blessing manifest
# whose pipelineConfigHash covers every gate script (audit SM14 F10).

